  "problem": "$\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1)=$",
  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{\u2218}<\\theta <{90}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $1$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where the tangent is positive.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061({45}^{\u2218})=1.\n$$\n\nSince ${45}^{\u2218}$ is an angle in the first quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1)={45}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
